WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/feedback/QueryError.tsx (+ its layout primitive _ErrorState.tsx) — the inline banner for a
  failed API query. It branches by ApiError.status so each failure mode gets actionable recovery copy:
    • !error                       → renders nothing (`return null`).
    • isTransientWaiting(error)    → Clock, role=status/polite, "Waiting for upstream", NO CTA (the global
                                     RateLimitBanner owns the countdown).
    • status === 404               → FileQuestion, "{{thing}} not found" (thing = resourceName ?? "Resource"),
                                     optional "Back to list" CTA when listHref is set → navigate(listHref).
    • status === 401 || 403        → Lock, "Sign in required", "Sign in" CTA → window.location.href='/login'.
    • status >= 500                → Server, "Server error", optional "Retry" CTA → onRetry.
    • network / offline / unknown  → WifiOff if offline else AlertCircle; isOffline = !online || status === 0;
                                     offline → role=status/polite "You're offline" + disabled "Retry when online";
                                     else role=alert/assertive "Can't reach server" + "Retry".
  A useEffect auto-invokes onRetry ONCE when the browser fires `online`, but ONLY for a pure transport failure
  (status === undefined) — a 4xx/5xx never recovers from a connectivity event, and status===0 is excluded.
  Data sources (hooks): useTranslation (→ P1/S10 facade), useNavigate (→ P4 nav seam), useOnlineStatus
  (→ the reactive `online` field of the P1/S8 snapshot). The `error` is a prop, mapped to a Shared-free
  classification at the seam.

